Subject: [PATCH] Add USDA Nutrition MCP server and wire into NutritionAgent
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- app/mcp_server.py: FastMCP server exposing two tools over stdio:
    search_food(query, page_size) — USDA FoodData Central text search
    get_ingredient_nutrients(name) — search + detail lookup, returns
    per-100g macros (calories, protein, fat, carbs, fiber, sugar, sodium)

- agents/nutrition_agent.py: NutritionAgent._fetch_usda_data_via_mcp
  opens one MCP stdio session per enrich_recipes call and queries the
  top two ingredients of every recipe in parallel. The returned USDA
  reference values are injected into the LLM prompt to ground per-serving
  estimates and raise confidence from "low" to "medium". NutritionNote
  carries a new usda_grounded flag. The whole MCP path is best-effort:
  silently returns {} when USDA_API_KEY is unset or the subprocess fails.

- schemas/nutrition.py: add usda_grounded: bool = False to NutritionNote

- requirements.txt: add mcp>=1.0.0,<2.0.0; loosen pydantic pin to
  >=2.11.0 (required by mcp 1.27+)

All 14 existing nutrition_agent unit tests pass unchanged.

